A simple decentralized match record application built with Solidity and deployed on the Ethereum Blockchain (Testnet).  
This project demonstrates how blockchain can ensure transparent, permanent, and tamper-proof recording of match results.  

📜 Project Description  

dailycheckin (MatchRecords) is a beginner-friendly smart contract that allows anyone to record and view match results transparently.  
Every match is stored permanently on the blockchain, ensuring no tampering or data loss.  
Perfect for recording results of eSports, sports tournaments, or any competitive event where trust and transparency matter.  

⚙️ What It Does  

- Anyone can record match results by entering Team A, Team B, and the Winner.  
- Each result is timestamped and stored immutably on-chain.  
- Users can view any recorded match and verify the authenticity of the results.  
- Ensures a transparent, trustless, and decentralized match record system.  

🌟 Features  

🧠 Simple & Beginner-Friendly – Clean Solidity structure, perfect for learning.  
🔗 Transparent Storage – Every result is visible and verifiable on-chain.  
📅 Time-Stamped Records – Each match result includes a block timestamp.  
⛓️ Immutable Data – Once saved, results cannot be changed or deleted.  
📢 Publicly Accessible – Anyone can view past match details anytime.  

📄 Smart Contract  

Language: Solidity ^0.8.0  
Framework: Remix / Hardhat compatible  
Network: Ethereum (Testnet)  
Deployed Transaction:  
